## Key items explained:

### For C:
- `*.o`, `*.obj` - Object files
- `*.exe`, `*.out` - Executables
- `*.so`, `*.dylib`, `*.dll` - Shared libraries
- `*.a`, `*.lib` - Static libraries
- `build/`, `dist/` - Build directories
- `*.gch`, `*.pch` - Precompiled headers

### For Emacs:
- `*~` - Backup files
- `\#*\#` - Auto-save files
- `.\#*` - Lock files
- `*.swp`, `*.swo`, `*.swn` - Vim swap files (often created alongside Emacs)
- `*.elc` - Compiled Emacs Lisp

## Minimal version (if you want just the essentials):

```gitignore
# C
*.o
*.obj
*.exe
*.out
*.so
*.dylib
*.a
*.lib
build/

# Emacs
*~
\#*\#
.\#*
*.swp
executable